1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,380
When you arrive at a hotel, go to the front desk.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,860
The staff may ask for your name, passport, reservation, and card.

3
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:10,380
You can say, "I have a reservation under Ogino."

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:13,980
In many hotels, the card is for extra costs.

5
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:18,600
These costs can be hotel food, a broken item, or other small fees.

6
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,960
The hotel may hold money, but it may not charge you now.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,700
After check-in, the staff gives you a room key or key card.

8
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:31,240
Ask about breakfast, Wi-Fi, and check-out time before you go upstairs.

9
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,280
Breakfast is not always included.

10
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:39,240
Some hotels also have an extra fee, so it is good to ask one clear question.

11
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,740
Hotel rooms can be different in other countries.

12
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:47,560
In Japan, rooms often have slippers, a toothbrush, and many small things.

13
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:51,320
In some Western hotels, the room may be simpler.

14
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:55,840
You may need to ask for a toothbrush, extra towels, or more toilet paper.

15
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:56,980
This is normal.

16
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:59,200
A short polite request is enough.

17
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,640
If something is wrong, call the front desk.

18
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,480
Say your room number first.

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:05,960
Then explain the problem in simple words.

20
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,780
You can say, "This is room 708.

21
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:10,820
The air conditioner is not working."

22
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,960
If there is broken glass, do not touch it.

23
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,020
Ask for housekeeping.

24
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:19,780
Risa checks in at a hotel and asks about her stay.

25
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:23,620
Later, she calls the front desk about a small room problem.

26
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,400
Good afternoon.

27
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:27,360
Welcome to Riverside Hotel.

28
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:28,640
How can I help you?

29
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,500
Risa: Hi.

30
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:32,760
I have a reservation under Ogino.

31
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:33,940
Thank you.

32
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:36,000
May I see your passport and card?

33
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,850
Risa: Sure.

34
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:38,720
Here you are.

35
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:39,520
Your room is ready.

36
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:41,000
You are in room 708.

37
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,020
Risa: Thank you.

38
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,120
Is breakfast included?

39
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:45,260
Yes.

40
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:46,840
Breakfast is from 7 to 10.

41
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:48,460
Risa: Great.

42
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,320
What is the Wi-Fi password?

43
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:53,320
It is written on your key card.

44
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,640
Risa: Thank you.

45
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,180
What time is check-out?

46
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,440
Check-out is at 11 a.m.

47
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,480
Risa: This is room 708.

48
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,060
The air conditioner is not working.

49
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:04,540
I am sorry about that.

50
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,980
Is the room too warm?

51
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:11,940
Risa: Yes, it is too warm.

52
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,140
Could someone check it?

53
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,240
Of course.

54
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,820
Someone will come in about ten minutes.

55
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:22,480
Risa: Thank you very much.
